        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tui): suppress unhandled rejection from async agent event handler",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `onAgentEvent` callback in `EmbeddedTuiBackend` calls `void this.handleAgentEvent(evt)` without a `.catch()` handler. Since `handleAgentEvent` is async and can reject, this creates an unhandled promise rejection that crashes the TUI process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd a noop `.catch(() => {})` to suppress the unhandled rejection, matching the pattern used elsewhere in the codebase for fire-and-forget async callbacks.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrevents the TUI from crashing when an agent event handler throws.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Behavior\nThe `onAgentEvent` callback now attaches a `.catch(() => {})` to the fire-and-forget `handleAgentEvent(evt)` promise.\n\n### Source\n`src/tui/embedded-backend.ts:325`\n```ts\nthis.unsubscribe = onAgentEvent((evt) => {\n  void this.handleAgentEvent(evt).catch(() => {});\n});\n```\n\n### Test output\n```\n$ pnpm test -- src/tui/embedded-backend.test.ts --run\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.tui.config.ts\n ✓ |tui| src/tui/embedded-backend.test.ts (41 tests) 3511ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  41 passed (41)\n   Duration  4.88s\n\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 14.29s\n```\n\n### Notes\n- This is a defensive fix; the callback is fire-and-forget by design.\n- The `.catch(() => {})` pattern is already used elsewhere for similar fire-and-forget handlers.\n- Existing tests continue to pass.",
        "branch": "fix/embedded-backend-void-async-catch",
